# Keep the Docker build context to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs
# (Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/). CI runs on a fresh checkout so the cost
# there is small, but the Dockerfile's own documented local invocation
# (`docker buildx build ... .`) would otherwise ship everything below to the
# daemon -- including, from a working checkout, gigabytes of build output and
# local agent scratch state that has no business in a build context.

# Rust build output -- regenerated inside the builder stage anyway.
target/

# Git history: not read by the build, and the largest thing here after target/.
.git/

# Local agent/tooling state, none of it an input to this build. `.claude/`
# in particular contains `worktrees/`, i.e. entire nested checkouts.
.claude/
.superpowers/
graft/

# Docker's own files: not inputs to the build they configure.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
